WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.359
Maya can't make it this afternoon.

00:00:03.128 --> 00:00:05.781
The coordinator reviews the change and confirms it.

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:09.048
One cancellation has now disrupted two commitments.

00:00:10.283 --> 00:00:13.270
This is KindHandoff, created by Shivam Gupta.

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:17.803
In this fictional household,

00:00:18.217 --> 00:00:21.696
Maya was going to pack Arun's library bag at two thirty,

00:00:21.706 --> 00:00:23.807
then drive him to book club at three.

00:00:23.817 --> 00:00:26.048
The ride depends on the bag being ready.

00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:34.514
Jo can enter the house between two and three, but cannot drive.

00:00:35.239 --> 00:00:38.851
Dev can drive, but is only free from two forty-five.

00:00:38.861 --> 00:00:42.937
The planner checks availability, capabilities, and conflicting commitments.

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:46.759
It proposes Jo for the bag and Dev for the ride.

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:53.270
A proposed plan is still only a proposal.

00:00:53.861 --> 00:00:56.337
The coordinator creates two handoff offers.

00:00:57.128 --> 00:00:59.870
Jo opens her private invitation and accepts the bag.

00:01:00.439 --> 00:01:02.759
Dev accepts the ride in his own session.

00:01:03.506 --> 00:01:07.092
Until each named helper accepts, the task stays uncovered.

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:14.981
Watch Dev's ride.

00:01:15.528 --> 00:01:18.203
It is accepted, but still waiting for the bag.

00:01:19.217 --> 00:01:20.848
Jo records the bag as packed.

00:01:21.461 --> 00:01:23.692
Only then does the ride become ready.

00:01:24.817 --> 00:01:26.314
Agreement and readiness stay separate,

00:01:26.439 --> 00:01:30.714
so an unfinished prerequisite cannot hide behind a name on the calendar.

00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:41.070
The handoff brief shows what changed and what remains.

00:01:42.106 --> 00:01:44.470
Dev acknowledges this specific revision.

00:01:45.328 --> 00:01:48.026
A later update does not rewrite that receipt.

00:01:48.994 --> 00:01:51.737
The circle can see who agreed, what is ready,

00:01:52.106 --> 00:01:54.203
and which version each person read.

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:02.962
The browser's bounded language simulator makes real MCP calls

00:02:02.972 --> 00:02:06.429
using the November twenty-fifth, twenty twenty-five protocol

00:02:06.439 --> 00:02:08.692
and Streamable HTTP.

00:02:09.772 --> 00:02:11.648
Activity shows the execution trace.

00:02:12.461 --> 00:02:15.514
Firebase provides sign-in and persistent household records.

00:02:16.306 --> 00:02:20.292
The simulator is deterministic; no live Alexa connection is claimed.

00:02:24.350 --> 00:02:30.692
KindHandoff starts with everyday support: bags, rides, meals, and visits.

00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:35.203
The pricing hypothesis is twelve dollars per household per month,

00:02:35.639 --> 00:02:37.003
with every helper included.

00:02:37.906 --> 00:02:39.626
Household validation comes next.

00:02:40.506 --> 00:02:42.617
Clear plans and accepted responsibility.
